= Solution
{parent=a}

With the <change of variables> $u=3+2x$, $du=2\,dx$, an <antiderivative> is
$$
\boxed{\int\frac{dx}{\sqrt{3+2x}}=\sqrt{3+2x}+C,\qquad x>-\frac32.}
$$
Here $C$ is the <constant of integration>.

= b
{parent=3}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

<Integration by parts> with $u=\ln x$ and $dv=x\,dx$ gives
$$
\boxed{\int x\ln x\,dx=\frac{x^2}{2}\ln x-\frac{x^2}{4}+C,\qquad x>0.}
$$
The remaining <integral> is $\frac12\int x\,dx$.

