If tangency occurs at $x_*$, the <slope> must satisfy both $k=2e^{2x_*}$ and $kx_*=e^{2x_*}$. Eliminating $k$ gives $2x_*=1$, so the <tangent through the origin to an exponential curve> has
$$
\boxed{k=2e.}
$$

= b
{parent=11}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The preceding <tangent line> calculation gives $x_*=1/2$ and $y_*=e^{2x_*}=e$. The point of tangency is
$$
\boxed{\left(\frac12,e\right).}
$$

